    {
      "id": "xbF3pnVuxdRgU9hgZHJYh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -72.57142857142878,
      "y": 997.8571428571431,
      "width": 1006.7040405273438,
      "height": 320,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b028",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1714328822,
      "version": 348,
      "versionNonce": 991243626,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1762292266006,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "  🤖 GenAI-First Principles:\n  • AI Orchestrator Pattern: Central LLM manager with provider abstraction (OpenAI, Anthropic, local Llama)\n  • Prompt Versioning: Track and A/B test prompts for scoring, feedback, and job matching\n  • Multi-Provider Fallback: GPT-4 → Claude → Local Llama chain for resilience\n  • Cost Optimization: Response caching (Redis), prompt compression, batch processing\n\n  🏗️ Software Engineering Best Practices:\n  • SOLID Principles: Single Responsibility (separate services), Open/Closed (pluggable AI providers), Dependency Inversion\n  • Clean Architecture: Domain Layer (entities, events) → Application Layer (use cases) → Infrastructure Layer (AI adapters)\n  • Domain-Driven Design: Domain events (InterviewSubmitted, CandidateScored), Event Sourcing, Aggregate roots\n\n  ⚡ Distributed Architecture:\n  • Microservices: Independent scaling | Async Communication: Message queues decouple producers/consumers\n  • Event-Driven: Pub/Sub pattern | Horizontal Scaling: Auto-scale by queue depth | Fault Tolerance: Retry logic, circuit breakers\n  • Idempotency: All endpoints and tasks | Observability: Distributed tracing, centralized logging, metrics\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "principles-box",
      "originalText": "  🤖 GenAI-First Principles:\n  • AI Orchestrator Pattern: Central LLM manager with provider abstraction (OpenAI, Anthropic, local Llama)\n  • Prompt Versioning: Track and A/B test prompts for scoring, feedback, and job matching\n  • Multi-Provider Fallback: GPT-4 → Claude → Local Llama chain for resilience\n  • Cost Optimization: Response caching (Redis), prompt compression, batch processing\n\n  🏗️ Software Engineering Best Practices:\n  • SOLID Principles: Single Responsibility (separate services), Open/Closed (pluggable AI providers), Dependency Inversion\n  • Clean Architecture: Domain Layer (entities, events) → Application Layer (use cases) → Infrastructure Layer (AI adapters)\n  • Domain-Driven Design: Domain events (InterviewSubmitted, CandidateScored), Event Sourcing, Aggregate roots\n\n  ⚡ Distributed Architecture:\n  • Microservices: Independent scaling | Async Communication: Message queues decouple producers/consumers\n  • Event-Driven: Pub/Sub pattern | Horizontal Scaling: Auto-scale by queue depth | Fault Tolerance: Retry logic, circuit breakers\n  • Idempotency: All endpoints and tasks | Observability: Distributed tracing, centralized logging, metrics\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nJeVwFZzVIdA7ZayB6K5V",
